==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Keiji''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Keiji''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Maeda Keiji has a lot of promising advantages. Firstly, he has a cheap cost and fast cooldown, allowing him to be used very flexibly. Additionally, this goes well with his [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Dark enemies, allowing him to be a disposable tanker against them. Keiji also packs a near-instant foreswing, making his damage output extremely reliable. Furthermore, Wave Immunity is nice to have, and lets Keiji completely wall [[Two Can]]. Finally, [[Strengthen]] doubles his damage output, which is a huge boost. Unfortunately, due to a lack of stats in his first two forms, Keiji can't utilize these advantages effectively.

It is strongly recommended to unlock Keiji's True Form if you plan to use him.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Keiji gains massive buffs in his True Form that completely remove his problem of low stats. Firstly, his HP is increased by nearly 50%, making him much sturdier. This goes well with a range increase to 320 range, now making him a midrange tank that can outrange melee pushers and effectively hide behind your meatshields, while still being able to tank for your backliners. His attack rate is also improved significantly, almost doubling his DPS. Finally, his Strengthen now activates earlier, making it easier to make use of his strong strengthened DPS.

As a generalist, Immortal Keiji is an amazing midranger. His DPS may be slightly low on paper, but this is more than made up for by Keiji's impressive bulk, and strong cost/cooldown stats, allowing him to get value easily. Besides, Strengthen completely patches Keiji's DPS issue. It is strongly recommended to boost Keiji past Lv.30 using [[Catseye]]s, as he is very stat-based and benefits immensely from the additional stats.

As for his niches, Keiji is also an excellent Dark tanker. His HP is already fantastic for how cheap he is and how often you could deploy him for, but Keiji's aforementioned offense lets him function as a strong bruiser, being able to duel with multiple Dark enemies. Furthermore, his range allows him to synergise well with Dark meatshields like [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]], allowing you to form a layered defense. This makes Keiji excellent for clearing [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP stages]], as well as other Dark-focused stages. Keiji also synergises well with other anti-Dark units, as he can tank for them. A good example of this is [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], who appreciates Keiji's tanking and returns the favour by Freezing aggressive Dark enemies. Both of these units even share a [[In Bloom (Combo)|Freeze Up Cat Combo]]. While his anti-Wave niche is not as important, Keiji still performs well in it, being able to brawl with almost all Wave Enemies in the game, and become an amazing counter to Two Can and [[Dark Dober]]. He is particularly useful in Wave stages where [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] may struggle in.

Overall, Keiji is an incredible unit to have!

==='''Talents'''===
Keiji's Talents are all very straight-forward. '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Weaken]]''' is situational as always, while everything else is a simple and direct improvement to Keiji's performance.

'''[[Strengthen]]''' is a strong boost to his damage output, improving his usage immensely, and it is recommended to go for it first.

'''Cost Down''' is inconsequential, since Keiji is already dirt cheap. It only reduces his cost by a meager 450¢, which is just not worth it no matter how you slice it.

'''HP Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' also improves Keiji's use by a large margin, as Keiji's stat-based nature means he benefits immensely from these buffs, though they are only recommended after you have boosted Keiji to Lv.50 using Catseyes.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Keiji's Ultra Talents add a lot to his kit. Starting with the new '''Target, Floating''' enemies typically have 2 characteristics that define them: short range, high damage. Keiji has the perfect blend of bulk and DPS to counter them effectively. His status as a midranger makes him the perfect pick over generic melee tankers when oppressive enemies prevent their usage, being especially decent in mixed stages.'''[[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]]''' transforms him a hard counter to [[Adherence to Virtue]] if you're struggling on that stage. Besides that, it does not find much applicability outside of [[Maawth]], [[I.M. Phace]], and [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and should only be unlocked after all other relevant talents are out of the way. Regardless, it acts as additional assurance that he doesn't get stunlocked in mixed stages.

Another feature that Keiji received was a '''[[Wave Attack]]''', occurring at a 20% activation rate. These Wave Attack pierce up to 733 range, improving his already high strengthened DPS. Through Wave Attacks, Keiji will have an average of 27K strengthened DPS; factoring in his Attack/Strengthen Up Talents would bring his average DPS to 40K, making him a phenomenal anti-Dark/Floating/generalist DPS. These Talents are a bit pricey for what they do, but you will not regret unlocking his Ultra Talents.

Additionally, it goes without saying that the stat increases and extra Orb slot from getting him to Lv.60 are already ridiculously good.

==='''Orb'''===
Resistant VS. Dark/Floating Orbs for tanking purposes, Berserker Orb for general damage due his high DPS. Resist weaken A-grade orb with same talent unlocked for immunity, only particularly helpful against Crocodylidae Kurocroc, effectively worthless everywhere else.

